CHAPTER.VERS:
The first place or part concerning comfort in afflictions, in which we should not be cast down and be faint hearted, but rather rejoice and be glad. My brethren,
Seeing their condition was miserable because of the scattering abroad, he does well to begin as he does. count it all joy
The first argument, because our faith is tried through afflictions: which ought to be most pure, for so it suits us. when ye fall into divers temptations;
